---
/**
 * The wordmark as inline SVG: "lion" in the inherited text colour, "ui" in the accent colour.
 *
 * It used to be public/lionui-text.svg loaded through <img>, with both colours baked in (white and
 * #FFC107) plus an `invert(1) hue-rotate(180deg)` filter for light mode. Two measured defects came
 * out of that: in the header the filter turned the accent into rgb(124,62,0) - a brown tint - and in
 * the footer, where no filter applied, the white half was invisible on the light page (255,255,255
 * pixels x2804). Inline, both halves follow the theme on their own and the filter can go.
 */
---
<svg
  class="logo-text-svg"
  width="86"
  height="36"
  viewBox="0 0 86 36"
  fill="none"
  role="img"
  aria-label="lion ui"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <text x="0" y="28" class="wordmark-glyphs" fill="currentColor">lıon</text>
  <!--
    The accent half carries its own grey rather than the accent token. It was var(--accent-yellow), and when that turned
    grey the wordmark followed it — but the mark's grey is a fixed part of the logo, measured as rgb(154, 160, 166) =
    #9aa0a6, and it reads the same on dark and light, which is the point of a literal here. Decoupled on purpose: the
    accent can be tuned ("can be lighter") without repainting the logo.
  -->
  <text x="54" y="28" class="wordmark-glyphs wordmark-accent" fill="#9aa0a6">uı</text>
</svg>

<style>
  .logo-text-svg {
    height: 36px;
    width: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .wordmark-glyphs {
    font-family: var(--font-family);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 32px;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  /*
   * No stroke on the accent half any more. It existed for one measured reason: the accent was #FFC107, which is 1.63:1
   * on the light bar and stops being readable as the chrome lightens, so a 1.5px 55%-black stroke sat behind the fill
   * to separate the letters from the background. The accent half is #9aa0a6 now, which needs no such help, and the
   * stroke was reading as an outline around the "ui" rather than as separation.
   */
</style>
